  "question": {
    "text": "All the values of $m$ for which both roots of the equations $x^2-2 m x+m^2-1=0$ are greater than $-2$ but less than 4 , lie in the interval"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n−2  < m < 0",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\nm > 3\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n−1  < m < 3",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n1  < m < 4",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Equation $x^2-2 m x+m^2-1=0$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& (x-m)^2-1=0 \\\\\n& (x-m+1)(x-m-1)=0 \\\\\n& x=m-1, m+1 \\\\\n& -2 < m-1 \\text { and } m+1 < 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n$m>-1$ and $m < 3$\n$-1 < m < 3$"
  }
}